#!/usr/bin/env sh
. "$(dirname -- "$0")/_/husky.sh"

# HUSKY HANDS THE WORK TO LEFTHOOK INSTEAD OF DOING ITS OWN.
#
# Measured 2026-09-07. `core.hooksPath` points at .husky, so git runs THIS file
# and never runs lefthook's pre-commit. lefthook says so on every commit --
# "Custom hooks paths are not supported by default", "Skipping hook sync" -- and
# nobody read it.
#
# The cost was five checks, not one: secrets, prettier, eslint, tsc and the
# no-cyrillic guard all live in lefthook.yml's pre-commit and none of them ran.
# A whole subsystem was written in Russian identifiers and committed clean,
# past a guard that exists and says "Write comments in English".
#
# It was worse than "nothing ran". This file used to call
# `pnpm exec lint-staged`, which fails on every commit with
# "Command lint-staged not found", and its exit code was never checked -- so the
# script printed "all checks passed" having run one check out of five. A gate
# that reports success while doing nothing is worse than no gate: it is a gate
# people trust.
#
# One line replaces all of it. `lefthook run pre-commit` executes what
# lefthook.yml declares, so there is one list of checks and one place to edit
# it. The secrets guard is not repeated here -- it is first in that list.
#
# WARNING FOR ANYONE RUNNING THIS BY HAND: `lefthook run pre-commit` restores
# files from the index when a check fails, and UNSTAGED edits are lost. It
# silently reverted two files during this very change. Commit first, then run
# hooks.
exec npx --no-install lefthook run pre-commit
